IMPORT prelude

-- The provision index of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory), reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- One entry per Part, Division, section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, the Schedule and each Part of the Schedule,
-- with its identifier as the text prints it and its heading as the text prints it.
-- Subsections, paragraphs and subparagraphs have no heading of their own: the heading carried is the heading of the section they stand in.
-- A paragraph of a definition in section 17 is identified by the defined term, as in 17 "bank"(a).
-- The two Divisions numbered 1 are told apart by their Part: Part VII, Division 1 and Part VIII, Division 1.
-- The entries were produced by a script that reads the text file: the table of provisions (lines 13 to 141) gives the section numbers and headings in order,
-- and the body (lines 149 to 962) is matched against it, so that the numbered items of examples are not taken for headings.
-- "line" is the line of the text file on which the provision starts.

DECLARE `Provision kind` IS ONE OF
    `a Part`
    `a Division`
    `a section`
    `a subsection`
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `the Schedule`
    `a Part of the Schedule`

DECLARE Provision HAS
    `identifier` IS A STRING
    `kind of provision` IS A `Provision kind`
    `heading` IS A STRING
    `line in the text file` IS A NUMBER

